  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Da vs Sanjay Kumar on 2 August, 2018 In The Court Of Samar Vishal, Additional Chief Metropolitan Magistrate-II, Patiala House Courts, New Delhi Cc No. 41265/2016 Date of Institution : 07.04.2008 Date of reserving judgement : 25.07.2018 Date of pronouncement : 02.08.2018 In re: Delhi Administration / Food Inspector Department of Pfa, Govt. of Nct of Delhi A-20, Lawrence Road Industrial Area, Delhi-110035 ... Complainant versus Sh. Sanjay Kumar S/o Sh. Nepali Singh Ajay Kiryana Store, Khasra No.1/24, Nathupura Road, Near Janta Medical Store, Burari. Delhi-84 R/o C/o Sh. Jai Parkash Tyagi, Mangal Bazax, Village Burari, Delhi-84 ... Accused Judgment: 1. The present is a complaint filed under section 16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 (herein after referred to as Pfa Act), alleging that the accused has violated the provisions of th",
    "facts": "2. As per the complaint, on 27.10.07 at about 4 PM, Food Inspector Gian Chand purchased a sample of \"Dal Arhar a food article for DA vs Sanjay Kumar analysis from accused Sanjay Kumar from the premises of Ajay Kiryana Store, Khasra No.1/24 Nathupura Road, Near Janta Medical Store, Burari. Delhi-84 where the said food article was found stored for sale and where accused Sanjay Kumar vendor was found conducting the business of the said food article at the time of sampling. Approx. 1500 gms. of Dal Arhar was taken from an open tin bearing no label or declaration. The sample was taken under the supervision/direction of Sh. Yogesh Pratap. SDM/LHA. The sample was taken after proper mixing the Dal Arhar with the help of a clean & dry Jhaba by rotating it in all possible directions. The Food Inspector divided the sample commodity into three equal parts then and there by putting them into three clean and dry glass bottles. Each sample bottle was separately packed, Da vs Sanjay Kumar on 2 August, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/67851671/ 1 fastened and sealed according to PFA Act 8. Rules. The vendor's signatures were obtained on me LHA slip and wrapper of the sample bottles. Notice in Form VI was given to Sh. Sanjay Kumar and the price of sample was also given to him vide vendor's receipt dated 27.10.07. Panchnama too was prepared at the spot. All the documents prepared by FI were signed by accused Sanjay Kumar and the other witness Sh. J.P. Bhardwaj, FA. Before starting sample proceedings efforts were made to join public witnesses but none tame forward. as such Sh. J.P. Bhardwaj. FA was joined as witness. 3. One counter-part of the sample bearing LHA Code Number 41/LHA/19827 was also sent to Public Analyst, Delhi in intact condition and remaining two counterparts were deposited with the SDM/LHA in intact conditions. Public AnaIyst analysed the sample and found the sample to be adulterated. The report of Public DA vs Sanjay Kumar Analyst is as follows: \"The sample is adulterated because it is coloured with synthetic colouring matter viz tartrazine\". 4. It is the case of the complainant that accused Sanjay Kumar was the vendor-cum-proprietor of Ajay Kiryana Store, Khasra No.1/24 Nathuputa Road, Near Janta Medical Store, Burari, Delhi-84 at the time of taking sample and as such he is in charge of and responsible for day to day conduct of the business of the said shop. The vendor did not disclose to the food inspector the name, address and other particulars of the person from whom he had purchased the article of food. 5. Thereafter on completion of investigation, sanction under section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA. The complaint was then filed in the court on 07.04.2008 alleging violation of section 2(ia)(j)&(m) and Rule 23 read with Rule 29 of PFA Rules, 1955 as punishable section 7/16(1)(a) of PFA Act against the accused. 6. As the complaint was filed in writing by a public servant, recording of pre-summoning evidence was dispensed with and the accused was summoned vide order dated 07.04.2008. Based on the report of the PA charge was framed against the accused for commission of the offence punishable under section 7/16(1) (a) PFA Act being violation of Section 2(ia)(a)(b)(j)&(m) of PFA Act and Rule 23 read with Rule 28 & 29 of PFA Rules, 1955, to which accused pleaded not guilty and claimed trial. DA vs Sanjay Kumar 7. At the trial, the prosecution examined four witness in support of its case i.e. PW-1 FI Gian Chand, PW-2 SDM/LHA Sh Yogesh Pratap, and PW-3 FA J.P. Bhardwaj. PW-1 and PW-3 were part of the team that had visited the spot for sample proceedings under the supervision of SDM/LHA Sh. Yogesh Pratap. These witness narrated the steps undertaken by them during the sample proceedings, including disclosing their identity, expressing intention to purchase sample for analysis, lifting the sample commodity of \"Arhar Dal\" 1.50 kg from the vendor for analysis, bearing no label or declaration, taking the sample of Arhar Dal and rotating in all directions, dividing the sample into three equal parts by putting them into three separate clean and dry sample bottles, separately sealing, packing and marking the same and obtaining signatures of vendor and witnesses. They also proved the necessary documents including the vendor's receipt Ex.PW- 1/A, Notice Ex. Da vs Sanjay Kumar on 2 August, 2018 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/67851671/ 2 PW-1/B, Panchnama Ex.PW-1/C. The accused also made statement Ex.PW1/D alongwith document. Thereafter, the remaining two counter parts of the sample in intact condition along with two copies of memo of Form VII in a sealed packet were deposited with LHA vide LHA Receipt Ex.PW1/F under intimation that one counterpart of the same has already been deposited with PA vide receipt Ex.PW1/E. Thereafter, PA Report Ex.PW1/H was received, according to which the sample found adulterated being coloured with synthetic colouring matter tatrazine. Thereafter the PW-1 FI Shri Gian Chand started the investigations and he sent a letter Ex. PW 1/I to VATO, Ward No. 72 and received its reply stating that the firm Ajay Kiryana Store was not registered in that Ward. Thereafter after completion of investigation, the entire case file including Public Analyst report DA vs Sanjay Kumar was submitted to Shri Mohan Lal, the then Director, PFA, who after applying his mind gave the consent Ex. PW 1/J. Thereafter the present complaint Ex. PW 1/K was filed by PW-4 FI D.V. Singh Then the intimation letter Ex.PW4/A alongwith PA report was sent to accused vide postal registration receipts Ex.PW4/B. These witnesses were duly cross-examined by Ld. Defence Counsel. 8. Statement of the accused under section 313 CrPC were recorded wherein the accused denied the allegations and pleaded innocence. Thereafter matter was listed for defence evidence. But the accused has not lead any defence evidence and matter was listed for final arguments.",
